---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Archex Craft Case Study — Archex Studio"
  description="How Archex Studio created the brand identity, typography hierarchy, and digital interface design system for Archex Craft."
  path="/archex-craft/"
>
  <div class="shell">
    <header class="page-intro">
      <div class="eyebrow" style="color: var(--signal); margin-bottom: 8px;">CASE STUDY // IN-HOUSE DESIGN SYSTEM</div>
      <h1 style="font-family: var(--serif); font-size: clamp(36px, 5vw, 64px); font-weight: 400; line-height: 1.1; margin: 0 0 16px;">
        Archex Craft<span style="color: var(--signal);">.</span>
      </h1>
      <p style="font-size: clamp(17px, 2vw, 20px); color: var(--graphite); max-width: 680px; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0;">
        Designing a brand identity and interface system for an engineering practice grounded in technical clarity, modularity, and structural precision.
      </p>
    </header>

    <!-- Case Study Summary Metrics Grid -->
    <section class="section reveal" style="padding-top: 32px; padding-bottom: 32px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);">
      <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(200px, 1fr)); gap: 24px;">
        <div>
          <span style="font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--graphite);">PRACTICE</span>
          <strong style="display: block; font-size: 16px; margin-top: 4px; color: var(--ink);">Archex Craft</strong>
        </div>
        <div>
          <span style="font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--graphite);">DISCIPLINES</span>
          <strong style="display: block; font-size: 16px; margin-top: 4px; color: var(--ink);">Brand Identity, UI/UX, Design Tokens</strong>
        </div>
        <div>
          <span style="font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--graphite);">DELIVERABLES</span>
          <strong style="display: block; font-size: 16px; margin-top: 4px; color: var(--ink);">Figma System, Code Tokens, Spec Guide</strong>
        </div>
        <div>
          <span style="font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--graphite);">PRODUCTION</span>
          <strong style="display: block; font-size: 16px; margin-top: 4px; color: var(--ink);">
            <a href="https://craft.archexweb.in" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--signal); text-decoration: underline;">
              craft.archexweb.in ↗
            </a>
          </strong>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Narrative Section 01: The Challenge -->
    <section class="section reveal" style="padding: 48px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);">
      <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(300px, 1fr)); gap: 40px; align-items: start;">
        <div>
          <span class="eyebrow">01 / THE CHALLENGE</span>
          <h2 style="font-family: var(--serif); font-size: clamp(28px, 3.5vw, 40px); font-weight: 400; margin: 12px 0 0; color: var(--ink);">
            Communicating engineering rigor without generic SaaS tropes.
          </h2>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p style="color: var(--graphite); line-height: 1.65; font-size: 16px; margin: 0 0 16px;">
            Most agency websites in the software space fall into two extremes: either visually cluttered with hyper-saturated neon gradients and floating 3D spheres, or dry and indistinguishable from basic utility documentation.
          </p>
          <p style="color: var(--graphite); line-height: 1.65; font-size: 16px; margin: 0;">
            For Archex Craft, the goal was to create a digital home that reads like a serious engineering workshop: calm, confident, tactile, and deeply structured. Every element needed to reflect how Craft approaches software delivery: purposeful, tested, and built to last.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Narrative Section 02: Design Decisions & Specimen -->
    <section class="section reveal" style="padding: 48px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);">
      <span class="eyebrow">02 / CORE DESIGN DECISIONS</span>
      <h2 style="font-family: var(--serif); font-size: clamp(28px, 3.5vw, 40px); font-weight: 400; margin: 12px 0 32px; color: var(--ink);">
        Three architectural design decisions.
      </h2>

      <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr)); gap: 24px;">
        <div style="background: var(--paper-soft); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 8px; padding: 28px;">
          <span style="font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 12px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--signal);">DECISION 01</span>
          <h3 style="font-size: 18px; font-weight: 600; margin: 8px 0 12px; color: var(--ink);">The Architectural Canvas</h3>
          <p style="font-size: 14px; color: var(--graphite); line-height: 1.6; margin: 0;">
            A dark-charcoal foundation with subtle grid lines reminiscent of blueprints. This gives code snippets, terminal commands, and system diagrams a native environment where technical details can be examined with high clarity.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div style="background: var(--paper-soft); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 8px; padding: 28px;">
          <span style="font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 12px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--signal);">DECISION 02</span>
          <h3 style="font-size: 18px; font-weight: 600; margin: 8px 0 12px; color: var(--ink);">Typographic Hierarchy</h3>
          <p style="font-size: 14px; color: var(--graphite); line-height: 1.6; margin: 0;">
            High-contrast pairing between crisp monospaced coordinates for data and status indicators, combined with a geometric sans-serif for headlines and dense, readable body text.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div style="background: var(--paper-soft); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 8px; padding: 28px;">
          <span style="font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 12px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--signal);">DECISION 03</span>
          <h3 style="font-size: 18px; font-weight: 600; margin: 8px 0 12px; color: var(--ink);">Design-to-Code Tokens</h3>
          <p style="font-size: 14px; color: var(--graphite); line-height: 1.6; margin: 0;">
            All spacing, radius, typography, and color decisions were documented as JSON design tokens mapped directly to Tailwind utility classes, guaranteeing zero translation loss during implementation.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Narrative Section 03: The Outcome & Live Link -->
    <section class="section reveal" style="padding: 48px 0;">
      <div style="background: #141414; color: #f2efe8; border-radius: 12px; padding: clamp(32px, 6vw, 64px); display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 24px;">
        <span style="font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 0.1em; color: var(--signal-bright); text-transform: uppercase;">03 / PRODUCTION OUTCOME</span>
        <h2 style="font-family: var(--serif); font-size: clamp(28px, 4vw, 44px); font-weight: 400; margin: 0; line-height: 1.2;">
          A cohesive digital identity live in production.
        </h2>
        <p style="color: #a29d93; max-width: 640px; font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.6; margin: 0;">
          Archex Craft now operates on this unified design system across its entire web presence, catalog, and documentation. You can explore the live implementation directly.
        </p>
        <div style="display: flex; gap: 16px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-top: 8px;">
          <a
            class="button on-dark"
            style="background: #f2efe8; color: #141414;"
            href="https://craft.archexweb.in"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >
            Visit Live Archex Craft Website ↗
          </a>
          <a
            class="button secondary"
            style="border-color: #4c4944; color: #f2efe8;"
            href="/work/"
          >
            ← Return to Selected Work
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>

  <section class="cta-band">
    <div class="cta-inner">
      <h2>Need a brand or interface designed with this care?</h2>
      <a class="button on-dark" href="/contact/">Discuss your design project <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
